\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{One edge}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Take two vertices joined by one edge of weight #{w>0}. The
operator #{-L_w} is #{w} times the matrix with diagonal entries #{1}
and off-diagonal entries #{-1}. The vector
#{\delta_a-\delta_b} is orthogonal to constant fields, and
#{-L_w} multiplies it by #{2w}. \ref{fdip-005U} therefore
sends that vector under #{(-L_w)^+} to itself divided by #{2w}.
The quadratic form equals #{\frac{1}{w}}. The
[effective conductance](fdip-00DF) equals #{w}. The energy of
the function with values #{1} and #{0} is the same number, and
that energy is the [kept form](fdip-00DF) on the two vertices.}
